User is reporting that their Computer is completely dead.

The user has conducted some troubleshooting:
- Pressed the power button several times
- Checked the wall outlet with another device (it works)
- Completely dead, no lights, no fan, no beep

Confirmed this as well by trying to remote in. No connection.

This could be a physical problem.
So this means we need to directly communicate with the user on site.

We ask the user to confirm it's truly dead.
Having them try a different outlet that's confirmed to work and a different power cable.
If no ligts or fan starts might indicate it needs to be replaced.

We get confirmation that none of the asked for methods yields any positive effect.
Thus device needs to be replaced.

We need the information from the user whether the Device is a Laptop or a Desktop as the replacement needs to match.
User confirmed Desktop.

I visit the Computer Deployment to build the replacement with "server imaging" (Customer Support agents need the imaged build, not Cloud Provisioning,
I will have to look into he Documentation -> Hardware & Assets -> "Choosing a PC Setup").

This demands I set up a replacement Device for the user and progressing through the set-up, making sure to follow the instructions
made by the deployment department.

We have to put the cables in the correct inputs.
then we press f12 to enter the install mode.
We choose in this scenario the PXE Network Boot IPv4(Onboard Gigabit Ethernet Controller) for the boot option.
We type in a password to progress and then have to edit the value to the name of the Device.

We give it the Value of:
SD2027

We then get to the log-in screen and by logging in, it should complete the set-up and it can be put on the shelf 
and ready to ship to the user as fast as possible.
Recommended to allow a return label in case they need to ship anything back to the IT department.

The new device is all working and ticket is closed.






