Computer naming convention
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Every machine name follows the SD asset convention: SD followed by four digits.
SD#### All workstations, desktop or laptop (examples SD1042, SD1108, SD1205)
This same SD#### value is the machine name AND its asset tag in inventory: one
identifier per device, so the asset register and the hostname always agree.
Rules:
Use the next free SD number. Check the asset register before assigning.
Names are uppercase, no spaces. Do not reuse a name already in the register.
Set the name in the wizard field OSDComputerName before the task sequence runs.

Procedure
------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Stage the hardware. Connect power, wired network, display, keyboard, and mouse.
The workstation powers on when mains power is connected.
2. Catch the boot menu. As the device powers on, tap F12 repeatedly until the
firmware boot menu appears.
3. Select the network boot. Choose PXE Network Boot IPv4. This site’s PXE serves
IPv4 only, so do not select the IPv6 entry; it will time out.
4. Authenticate. When the Deployment Wizard loads, enter the deployment password
(Deploy#2026). No user name is required.
5. Name the machine. On the Task Sequence Wizard, press Edit and set OSDComputerName
to the assigned name from Section 5. Confirm the value, then OK and Next.
6. Run the task sequence. Start the Imaging Server task sequence. It partitions the
disk, applies the image, installs applications, and joins the domain without further
input. Do not power off during this stage.
7. Reboot. The machine restarts automatically when imaging completes.
8. Verify sign-in. At the logon screen, sign in with your domain credentials
(Section 4) to confirm the build.
